{"id": "building-jobs-and-change-orders", "title": "Building jobs grow by change order; the City still does not score how its builders perform", "seconds": 148.0, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "27704cbedbc3c208", "words": 472, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "When a San Francisco building job runs over, is it the builder? Or the City?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.9, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Who runs over?", "sub": "City construction contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.2, 0.38, 0.83, 1.13, 1.36, 1.6, 2.24, 2.41, 2.5, 2.59, 3.12, 3.3, 3.41]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "In May 2026, the Board’s Budget and Legislative Analyst reported.", "t0": 4.9, "t1": 8.66, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "297 construction contracts, five departments, July 2021 to June 2024"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.48, 0.73, 1.32, 1.45, 1.75, 2.1, 2.23, 2.69, 3.07]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "It totaled the change orders on 297 City building contracts.", "t0": 8.78, "t1": 11.84, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "297 construction contracts, five departments, July 2021 to June 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 0.56, 0.83, 1.09, 1.2, 1.36, 1.57, 2.04, 2.26, 2.51]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[2]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "186.8 million dollars, in three years.", "t0": 11.96, "t1": 14.68, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$186.8 million", "label": "added by approved change orders, July 2021 to June 2024", "sub": "8% on top of the first contract value"}, "emph": ["186.8"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.45, 0.92, 1.13, 1.32, 1.61, 1.96, 2.12, 2.36]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "status"], "text": "A change order adds work or money to a signed contract. These are official findings, by the City’s own auditors.", "t0": 15.2, "t1": 20.74, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A change order", "sub": "more work or money on a signed contract"}, "emph": ["official findings"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.37, 0.6, 0.83, 1.08, 1.23, 1.45, 1.55, 1.61, 1.89, 2.84, 3.06, 3.17, 3.51, 4.34, 4.48, 4.58, 4.85, 5.03]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "They also found the law requires a database scoring builders.", "t0": 20.96, "t1": 23.39, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a contractor evaluation database that the law requires and departments do not use"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.34, 0.59, 0.7, 0.89, 1.26, 1.32, 1.69, 2.0]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Departments don’t use it. So no one can say who runs over.", "t0": 23.51, "t1": 26.07, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a contractor evaluation database that the law requires and departments do not use"}, "emph": ["don’t use it"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.56, 0.77, 1.21, 1.4, 1.51, 1.62, 1.76, 1.95, 2.09, 2.32]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[5]", "timeline[2]", "established[9]"], "text": "A Civil Grand Jury asked that departments start entering those scores by the end of 2022.", "t0": 26.19, "t1": 30.27, "shot": "b4g", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "We recommend that by 12/31/2022, the Mayor require all Chapter 6 departments to begin submitting evaluations into the database.", "kicker": "Civil Grand Jury, “Shovel Ready”"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 0.63, 0.95, 1.21, 1.39, 1.81, 2.06, 2.33, 2.47, 2.8, 2.92, 3.03, 3.19, 3.27, 3.54]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["established[5]", "established[8]"], "text": "The Controller’s 2025 status table gives the answer: it will not be implemented.", "t0": 30.39, "t1": 34.64, "shot": "b4h", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["will not be implemented"], "sub": "the Controller’s 2025 status table"}, "emph": ["will not be implemented"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.57, 0.82, 1.3, 1.65, 2.02, 2.24, 2.36, 3.18, 3.31, 3.46, 3.61, 3.72]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "Take Crystal Springs/San Andreas, built by Kiewit Infrastructure West Company.", "t0": 35.26, "t1": 38.6, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["original amount", "$99,763,000"], "b": ["final amount", "$132,421,418"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.57, 0.9, 1.1, 1.62, 1.84, 1.97, 2.26, 2.77, 2.96]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "The Controller’s close-out: 99.8 million at the start, 132.4 million at the end.", "t0": 38.72, "t1": 44.39, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["original amount", "$99,763,000"], "b": ["final amount", "$132,421,418"]}, "emph": ["132.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.48, 1.48, 1.94, 2.16, 2.35, 2.65, 2.72, 2.82, 3.71, 3.88, 4.1, 4.5, 4.72, 4.92, 5.21, 5.3, 5.4]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[5]"], "text": "The Central Subway’s main contract, with Tutor Perini Corporation,", "t0": 44.51, "t1": 47.72, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Central Subway", "kicker": "Tutor Perini Corporation", "sub": "awarded at $839.7 million; $1.20 billion at Modification No. 147"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.4, 0.77, 1.01, 1.52, 1.69, 1.96, 2.28]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[5]"], "text": "was awarded at 839.7 million dollars.", "t0": 47.72, "t1": 50.72, "shot": "b6c", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Central Subway", "kicker": "Tutor Perini Corporation", "sub": "awarded at $839.7 million; $1.20 billion at Modification No. 147"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.56, 0.7, 0.88, 1.13, 1.59, 1.83, 2.1, 2.36]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[5]"], "text": "How many change orders followed?", "t0": 50.84, "t1": 51.99, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Central Subway", "kicker": "Tutor Perini Corporation", "sub": "awarded at $839.7 million; $1.20 billion at Modification No. 147"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.26, 0.51, 0.75]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "671.", "t0": 51.99, "t1": 53.03, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "671", "label": "change orders on the Central Subway contract", "sub": "$1.20 billion at Modification No. 147"}, "emph": ["671"], "wt": [0.04, 0.25, 0.47]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "Its federal profiles: 31 percent complete in January 2015, 69 by December 2017.", "t0": 53.55, "t1": 59.45, "shot": "b7a", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Central Subway, percent complete in the federal profiles", "rows": [["January 2015", "31%"], ["December 2015", "53%"], ["December 2016", "64%"], ["December 2017", "69%"]]}, "emph": ["69"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.5, 1.42, 1.81, 2.11, 2.49, 2.62, 2.95, 3.17, 4.07, 4.56, 4.68, 5.14, 5.39]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "Gains of 22, then 11, then 5 points a year. Every profile kept the 1.58 billion cost.", "t0": 59.57, "t1": 65.96, "shot": "b7a", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Central Subway, percent complete in the federal profiles", "rows": [["January 2015", "31%"], ["December 2015", "53%"], ["December 2016", "64%"], ["December 2017", "69%"]]}, "emph": ["1.58 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.35, 1.1, 1.28, 1.83, 2.03, 2.24, 2.47, 2.54, 3.51, 3.75, 4.16, 4.33, 4.43, 4.59, 4.81, 5.1, 5.34, 5.73]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Van Ness: its core bus project, 125.6 million in 2012.", "t0": 66.08, "t1": 71.3, "shot": "b7b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Van Ness core bus project, November 2012", "$125.6 million"], "b": ["At its highest, October 2016", "$189.5 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 1.05, 1.27, 1.57, 1.81, 2.71, 2.87, 3.07, 3.5, 3.74, 4.01, 4.41, 4.58, 4.84]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "At its highest, 189.5 million.", "t0": 71.42, "t1": 73.67, "shot": "b7bx", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Van Ness core bus project, November 2012", "$125.6 million"], "b": ["At its highest, October 2016", "$189.5 million"]}, "emph": ["189.5 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.27, 0.63, 0.8, 1.06, 1.47, 1.69, 1.92]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Opening was set for 2018. Service began in April 2022.", "t0": 73.79, "t1": 77.25, "shot": "b7c", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Opening: 2018, then April 2022", "kicker": "Van Ness Improvement Project", "sub": "set for 2018 in the 2014 profile; service began April 2022"}, "emph": ["April 2022"], "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.43, 0.61, 0.74, 1.01, 1.79, 2.08, 2.32, 2.41, 2.71, 2.96]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].what"], "text": "The Biosolids Digester project went from 1.68 billion to 2.84 billion dollars.", "t0": 77.37, "t1": 82.62, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2020-12", "to": "2026-06", "days": "", "fromLab": "$1.68 billion", "toLab": "$2.84 billion, finish +20 months", "kicker": "SEP Biosolids Digester Facilities Project"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.71, 1.15, 1.49, 1.66, 1.86, 2.03, 2.45, 2.7, 2.87, 3.54, 3.71, 3.92, 4.14, 4.32, 4.54, 4.83]}, {"scene": "jobs", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Why did prices change? In the City’s own words, mostly work the City added, and delay, claims and settlements.", "t0": 82.74, "t1": 87.87, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Added, by the reason the item prints", "rows": [["work the owner added or changed", "$200.1 million"], ["delay, claims and settlements", "$199.4 million"], ["prices and bids", "$115.9 million"], ["conditions found on site", "$43.7 million"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.28, 0.65, 1.41, 1.54, 1.64, 1.91, 2.05, 2.36, 2.63, 2.79, 2.9, 3.15, 3.73, 3.9, 4.18, 4.49, 4.59]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "So does it follow the builder?", "t0": 88.09, "t1": 89.84, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Needed increases, against the department’s rate", "rows": [["Sierra Mountain Construction Inc", "6 of 14"], ["Pilot Construction Management Inc", "3 of 12"], ["Mitchell Engineering", "4 of 8"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.37, 0.45, 0.7, 0.78]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "Three firms ran over more often than their department:", "t0": 89.84, "t1": 92.35, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Needed increases, against the department’s rate", "rows": [["Sierra Mountain Construction Inc", "6 of 14"], ["Pilot Construction Management Inc", "3 of 12"], ["Mitchell Engineering", "4 of 8"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.63, 0.79, 0.99, 1.18, 1.44, 1.56, 1.69]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "Sierra Mountain Construction, Pilot Construction Management, Mitchell Engineering.", "t0": 92.35, "t1": 96.3, "shot": "b11x", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Needed increases, against the department’s rate", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Sierra Mountain Construction Inc", "sub": "6 of 14"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Pilot Construction Management Inc", "sub": "3 of 12"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Mitchell Engineering", "sub": "4 of 8"}]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.39, 0.63, 1.54, 1.89, 2.3, 3.15, 3.47]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "But among 43 builders, chance alone would produce about that many.", "t0": 96.42, "t1": 99.92, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Needed increases, against the department’s rate", "rows": [["Sierra Mountain Construction Inc", "6 of 14"], ["Pilot Construction Management Inc", "3 of 12"], ["Mitchell Engineering", "4 of 8"]]}, "emph": ["chance"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.79, 1.6, 1.89, 2.17, 2.34, 2.61, 2.82, 3.02]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "It follows the department instead.", "t0": 100.04, "t1": 101.47, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Recreation and Park", "33%"], "b": ["Port", "3%"], "kicker": "Added by change orders, by department"}, "emph": ["department"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.47, 0.55, 0.96]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[4]"], "text": "Change orders added 33 percent at Recreation and Park, 3 percent at the Port.", "t0": 101.59, "t1": 105.67, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Recreation and Park", "33%"], "b": ["Port", "3%"], "kicker": "Added by change orders, by department"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.58, 0.8, 1.19, 1.54, 1.66, 2.17, 2.27, 2.99, 3.23, 3.52, 3.62, 3.72]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[7]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "And on 3 low-bid contracts, City payments now pass what the runner-up bid.", "t0": 105.79, "t1": 109.74, "shot": "b_runnerup", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid past the runner-up’s bid", "rows": [["Bay Area Lightworks, signal contract No. 36", "bid $3,443,384 · paid $5,714,337"], ["Hoseley Corporation, Pier 94 Backlands", "bid $6,712,203 · paid $7,528,472"], ["Chiang C.M. Construction, Rent Board fit-out", "bid $1,408,768 · paid $1,589,563"]], "kicker": "3 of 39 low-bid contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.6, 0.92, 1.78, 2.09, 2.43, 2.64, 2.99, 3.14, 3.25, 3.61]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[13]"], "text": "Public Works added five locations to the signal contract after the original bids.", "t0": 109.86, "t1": 113.49, "shot": "scope-signal_change", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Original bids and final payments", "heading": "Traffic-signal contract 36", "source": "signal_change", "rows": [{"icon": "lease", "label": "Original contract", "value": "$3,443,384"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "Added authority", "value": "$2,754,707.20"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.53, 0.78, 1.02, 1.51, 1.63, 1.73, 2.02, 2.42, 2.66, 2.75, 3.08]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[13]"], "text": "At Pier 94, the award included an alternate. Payments stayed within the original authorization.", "t0": 113.61, "t1": 118.65, "shot": "scope-pier94_award", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Original bids and final payments", "heading": "Pier 94", "source": "pier94_award", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Award including alternate", "value": "$6,969,003"}, {"icon": "vote", "label": "With contingency", "value": "$7,665,903"}, {"icon": "transfer", "label": "Recorded payments", "value": "$7,528,472"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.39, 1.16, 1.28, 1.53, 1.94, 2.05, 3.0, 3.52, 3.81, 4.02, 4.11, 4.42]}, {"scene": "builder", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[7]", "established[13]"], "text": "The Rent Board project also changed. The commission approved additional contingency.", "t0": 118.77, "t1": 122.2, "shot": "scope-rentboard_change", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Original bids and final payments", "heading": "Rent Board", "source": "rentboard_change", "rows": [{"icon": "transfer", "label": "Recorded payments", "value": "$1,589,563"}, {"icon": "vote", "label": "Approved limit", "value": "$1,619,538.41"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.52, 0.88, 1.16, 1.46, 1.56, 1.89, 2.23, 2.58]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[10]"], "text": "A 2011 review found change orders across eight departments, without a central database.", "t0": 122.42, "t1": 126.78, "shot": "record-10-218 contracts", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ov11co", "text": "218 contracts", "mark": "218 contracts", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.67, 0.99, 1.22, 1.52, 1.78, 2.12, 2.29, 3.03, 3.32, 3.38, 3.69]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[11]"], "text": "The later contractor database contained few completed evaluations.", "t0": 126.9, "t1": 130.01, "shot": "record-11-12 of 176 projects", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ov24pw", "text": "12 of 176 projects", "mark": "12 of 176 projects", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.81, 1.19, 1.61, 1.82, 2.22]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[12]"], "text": "A proposal to require departments to consider evaluations went no further.", "t0": 130.13, "t1": 133.24, "shot": "record-12-File 221268", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ov24pw", "text": "File 221268", "mark": "File 221268", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.54, 0.64, 0.96, 1.37, 1.45, 1.79, 2.41, 2.6, 2.75]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "No finding says any builder was overpaid. Which builders run over most stays unknown.", "t0": 133.46, "t1": 137.33, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any builder was overpaid, or any change order unjustified", "Which builders run over most"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.56, 0.73, 0.88, 1.11, 1.23, 2.1, 2.33, 2.68, 2.84, 3.02, 3.18, 3.47]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? Every change order, contract by contract, with its reason.", "t0": 137.45, "t1": 141.22, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each change order by contract: dollars, days and reason"}, {"who": "", "what": "Close-outs at Public Works and the Airport"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0